# Public keys trusted to sign Blankee releases, in ssh allowed-signers format.
#
# install.sh copies this to /etc/blankee/allowed_signers on a new installation
# and never overwrites it afterwards, and the updater never rewrites it either.
# That is deliberate. If this file were refreshed from the repository on every
# update, an attacker who could push a release could swap the key along with the
# code and the signature would prove nothing. Pinned once, it means a machine
# already installed cannot be taken over by pushing to the repository alone -
# the signing key is needed as well.
#
# Rotating a key therefore takes a human on each machine. That is the cost of
# the guarantee, and it is the right way round.
